  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1257 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nWednesday may need another Heat Advisory for the same locations as\nTuesday, but Thursday and Friday look \"slightly\" drier in terms of\nafternoon mixing, so heat indices may be limited a bit more and\nand advisory probably won't be needed. Starting on Friday and\nstretching into the first couple days of August, the ridge should\nslide further west over the desert Southwest, opening the door for\nmore north to northeasterly mid-level flow over south central\nTexas. A weak disturbance or two may ride southward within this\nnortherly flow and bring a chance at shower or isolated\nthunderstorms this weekend into the following week, but odds are\nlow at this time. The primary concern will continue to be the heat\nas we enter the Climatologically hottest 2 week stretch of the\nyear through mid-August.",
